# Sherpa Project Patterns

## Stack

- Next.js 16 (App Router, RSC, React 19)
- TypeScript strict mode
- Tailwind CSS 4 + shadcn/ui (new-york style, zinc base)
- Framer Motion (`motion/react`) for animations
- Deployment: Cloudflare Workers via OpenNext (`yarn deploy`)
- Package manager: Yarn 4 via Corepack (`packageManager: yarn@4.5.0`) — do NOT add `yarn` as a npm dependency

## Architecture: Feature-Sliced Design

```
src/
├── app/              # Routes only — thin pages, no business logic
├── features/         # Domain features (activity, database, home, timeline)
│   └── <feature>/components/   # Feature-scoped components
├── components/
│   ├── common/       # Shared reusable (CyberComponents, ThemeProvider, etc.)
│   ├── layout/       # Shell components (TopNav, MusicPlayer, ScrollToTop)
│   └── ui/           # shadcn/ui primitives (do NOT edit manually)
├── data/             # JSON content + dynamic loaders
├── hooks/            # Custom React hooks
├── lib/              # Utilities (cn, page-utils, audio, bungie API)
├── config/           # App constants (nav items — lightweight, not full JSON)
├── types/            # Shared TypeScript interfaces
└── store/            # Global state
```

## Rules

### 1. Route Pages Are Thin

Route files (`src/app/**/page.tsx`) must be minimal — delegate to `createActivityPage()` or render a feature component. No inline business logic.

```tsx
// ✅ Correct
export default async function RaidPage({ params, searchParams }: PageProps) {
  return await createActivityPage(params, searchParams, getRaidData)
}
```

### 2. Data-Driven Content + Dynamic Imports

All game content lives in `src/data/` as JSON. Never hardcode game content in components. Never import JSON statically at module level (especially not from `"use client"` pages).

To add activity content:
1. Create JSON in the right subfolder (`raids/`, `dungeons/`, `exotic-missions/`, `pantheon/`, `timeline/`)
2. Add slug to the registry array in `src/data/index.ts`
3. Add dynamic import entry + loader in the same file

```tsx
// ✅ Correct — code-split per slug
export async function getRaidData(slug: string): Promise<ActivityData | null> {
  const loader = raidImports[slug]
  if (!loader) return null
  const mod = await loader()
  return mod.default as unknown as ActivityData
}

// ❌ Wrong — pulls entire JSON into the client bundle
import data from "@/data/database/exotic-weapons.json"
```

Database/timeline pages must follow the same dynamic-loader pattern (server load → props, or dynamic `import()`), not static JSON imports.

### 3. Type Safety

- All data shapes in `src/types/index.ts` (`ActivityData`, `ActivityEncounter`, `LootWeapon`, …)
- Allow `[key: string]: unknown` for forward-compatible JSON fields
- Props interfaces live in the same file as the component
- Prefer early returns / local consts over non-null assertions (`!.`)
- Avoid long inline casts — extract a small local type or assign once after a guard

### 4. Component Patterns

```tsx
"use client" // Only when component uses hooks/interactivity

import { motion, AnimatePresence } from "motion/react"
import { SomeType } from "@/types"

interface MyComponentProps {
  data: SomeType
}

export function MyComponent({ data }: MyComponentProps) {
  // ...
}
```

- Named exports only (no default exports for components)
- `"use client"` only when needed (hooks, event handlers, motion)
- Imports use `@/` path alias
- Deduplicate repeated JSX with tiny local helpers in the same file (e.g. `PerkRow`, `EpicList`) — do not over-abstract into new packages
- Style: no semicolons, consistent with existing cleaned files

### 5. Activity Guide Views

Every activity guide view that uses `GuideSidebar` must also mount `MobileGuideTOC` (sidebar returns `null` on mobile):

```tsx
<GuideSidebar groups={sidebarGroups} title={pageTitle} ... activeEncounterId={currentViewId} />
<MobileGuideTOC groups={sidebarGroups} activeEncounterId={currentViewId} title={pageTitle} />
```

- Derive shared values once (`pageTitle`, `currentViewId`, `isOverview`, …) — do not repeat ternaries in JSX
- `useMemo` sidebar `groups` when passed into effects that sync TOC context

### 6. Styling

- Tailwind utility classes exclusively
- Design system: `CyberComponents.tsx` + CVA variants
- CyberVariants: `cyan | orange | yellow | red | green | zinc | exotic`
- Neon tokens: `neon-cyan`, `neon-orange`, `neon-yellow`, `neon-red`, `neon-green`
- Theme tokens: `src/lib/theme.ts` (`getTheme`, `ThemeColor`)
- `cn()` from `@/lib/utils` for conditional classes
- Dark-first (default theme is dark)
- Do NOT manually edit `src/components/ui/` (shadcn)

### 7. Animations

Use Framer Motion (`motion/react`) with the standard page transition:

```tsx
<AnimatePresence mode="wait">
  <motion.div
    key={uniqueKey}
    initial={{ opacity: 0, y: 10 }}
    animate={{ opacity: 1, y: 0 }}
    exit={{ opacity: 0, y: -10 }}
    transition={{ duration: 0.2, ease: "easeInOut" }}
  >
    {content}
  </motion.div>
</AnimatePresence>
```

### 8. Shared Utilities

- `cn()` → `@/lib/utils`
- Activity page factory → `@/lib/page-utils` (`createActivityPage`)
- Background audio → `@/lib/audio` (`playGlobalBgAudio`) — do not duplicate `getElementById("global-bg-audio")`
- Bungie image URLs → prefer a local `bungieUrl(path)` helper when repeating `https://www.bungie.net${path}`

### 9. API Routes

- Validate/sanitize all request input
- Cap payload size (e.g. TTS text length)
- Allowlist enums (e.g. TTS voices) — never interpolate untrusted strings into SSML/XML attributes
- Prefer direct dependencies over relying on unused transitive packages

### 10. Language & Naming

- UI text: Vietnamese
- Code (variables, types, comments): English
- Files/folders: English, kebab-case

| Type | Convention | Example |
|------|-----------|---------|
| Components | PascalCase | `ActivityEncounterView.tsx` |
| Hooks | kebab-case + `use-` | `use-scroll-spy.ts` |
| Data files | kebab-case | `vault-of-glass.json` |
| Utils/lib | kebab-case | `page-utils.tsx`, `audio.ts` |
| Types | PascalCase interfaces | `ActivityData` |

### 11. Performance

- Remote `bungie.net` images → `next/image` with width/height
- Prefer Server Components; `"use client"` only when needed
- Lazy-load heavy UI with `next/dynamic` when appropriate
- Keep nav metadata in `src/config/constants.ts` — never load full activity JSON just for menus

### 12. Adding a New Activity Type

1. Extend/create type in `src/types/index.ts`
2. Add JSON under `src/data/<type>/`
3. Register slug + dynamic import + loader in `src/data/index.ts`
4. Thin route at `src/app/<type>/[slug]/page.tsx` via `createActivityPage()` (or equivalent)
5. Mount both `GuideSidebar` + `MobileGuideTOC` in the feature view
6. Add nav entry in `src/config/constants.ts` / TopNav

### 13. Deploy & Tooling

```bash
yarn check          # lint:fix + tsc --noEmit
yarn deploy         # opennextjs-cloudflare build && wrangler deploy
```

- Use Yarn 4 via Corepack (`corepack enable` / `corepack prepare yarn@4.5.0 --activate`)
- Do not commit `.env`, `.next/`, `out/`, or secrets
